name issue_21_shallow_drop_repair
describe Shallow bottleneck buffer (20 ms) with a 3x capacity drop: repair traffic must follow the measured repair share, as in libwebrtc (issue #21)
compare_seeds 80
duration 40s
at 0s  capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=20ms
at 10s capacity=500kbps
at 25s capacity=1500kbps
# The encoder budget takes off the share that RTX and FEC really used in the
# last second, capped at 50%, as libwebrtc's FecControllerDefault does
# (compare/webrtc/reference/modules/video_coding/fec_controller_default.cc,
# UpdateFecRates). Without it the 20 ms queue overflows at the drop and repair
# traffic piles on top of the video. Bounds hold on seeds 1-20 (max 94.9 and
# 2.8); main (c88105d) on seed 1 has 100.4 and 3.6, and up to 253 and 12 over
# the 20 seeds.
# libwebrtc has no value for this scenario yet (it is not in the sm_compare
# suite); on capacity_drop it has repair overhead 2.9 % and loss 1.4 %.
expect repair.overhead_pct < 100
expect video.residual_loss_pct < 3
expect audio.interruptions <= 1
